:glossary.Glossary
:gl.
:grpsep.C
:gt.Constellation Diagram
:gd.A diagram that displays amplitude and phase for various digital
modulation modes, including PSK and QAM.
:gt.CSS
:gd.Chirp Spread-Spectrum, a modulation mode often used for ISM band
devices
:grpsep.I
:gt.ISM Band
:gd.Various unlicensed radio bands that permit some amount of transmit
power, but barely any; almost all of them (except for the 40 MHz band
in most countries) overlap amateur radio bands.
:grpsep.L
:gt.LoRa
:gd.:q.Long Range:eq., a CSS modulation mode with very good SNR
:grpsep.O
:gt.OSI Model
:gd.A reference model for a network stack also called the OSI Stack,
which is often applied to other protocols. The layers are physical,
data-link, network, transport, session, presentation, application
:grpsep.P
:gt.PSK
:gd.:q.Phase-Shift Keying:eq., a data modulation mode in which the
phase of the signal is modulated
:grpsep.Q
:gt.QAM
:gd.:q.Quadrature Amplitude Modulation:eq., a data modulation mode
where the amplitude and phase of the modulated analog waveform is varied
:grpsep.S
:gt.SNR
:gd.:q.Signal-to-Noise Ratio:eq., a ratio of the signal strength to the
noise strength
:egl.
:index.
:euserdoc.
